# Keeps the Docker build context (docker/samba-mount's Dockerfile does
# `COPY . .` then builds fresh with cargo inside the container) down to
# just the source the build actually needs. Without this, `target/` alone
# (regenerated fresh in the container anyway - stale host build artifacts
# are never useful there) balloons the context into gigabytes.
/target/
/.git/
/.local/
